# =============================================================================
# AI Market Agent — example configuration
#
# Copy to .env and fill in. NEVER commit .env (it is gitignored).
# Every default here is the safe option: an empty .env cannot touch real money.
# =============================================================================

NODE_ENV=development
LOG_LEVEL=info
LOG_PRETTY=true

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TRADING MODE
#
#   backtest  historical simulation only
#   paper     simulated portfolio against live data  (default)
#   live      real money  — requires everything in the LIVE block below
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
MODE=paper
PAPER_TRADING=true
LIVE_TRADING=false

# Live trading additionally requires ALL of the following:
#   MODE=live
#   LIVE_TRADING=true
#   PAPER_TRADING=false
#   LIVE_TRADING_CONFIRMATION=I_UNDERSTAND_REAL_MONEY_RISK
#   a non-empty ALLOWED_ASSETS list
#   risk limits within sane bounds (see src/config/env.ts)
# The process refuses to start if any of these is missing.
LIVE_TRADING_CONFIRMATION=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# INSTRUMENT PERMISSIONS — all disabled by default
#
# In live mode the bot may only ever place orders on instruments listed in
# ALLOWED_ASSETS. In every mode, including paper, the Risk Engine refuses a
# symbol whose instrument class is switched off below: a crypto pair such as
# DOGE/USD is rejected while ALLOW_CRYPTO=false, and an option contract needs
# ALLOW_OPTIONS *and* ALLOW_DERIVATIVES. The classifier recognises explicit
# pair notation (DOGE/USD, DOGE-USD) and OCC option symbols; a concatenated
# DOGEUSD is indistinguishable from a ticker and is NOT caught, which is why
# ALLOWED_ASSETS — an allowlist, not a pattern — stays the control for live.
#
# It has no capability to withdraw funds, transfer money, change bank details,
# or open accounts: no such code path exists anywhere in this repository.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
ALLOWED_ASSETS=
ALLOW_CRYPTO=false
ALLOW_OPTIONS=false
ALLOW_DERIVATIVES=false
ALLOW_MARGIN=false
ALLOW_SHORT_SELLING=false
MAX_LEVERAGE=1

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RISK LIMITS (percentages of portfolio value)
# Enforced by the Risk Engine, which is independent of the LLM and can veto any
# signal the model produces.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Paper/backtest portfolio size. Larger than the live target on purpose: at a
# few hundred euros, position sizes are swamped by commission and spread, so
# paper results measure costs rather than signal quality (docs/SPEC_ADAPTATIONS.md).
PAPER_CAPITAL_EUR=10000
# Real money that would actually be at risk if live trading were ever enabled.
LIVE_CAPITAL_EUR=300
BASE_CURRENCY=EUR
MAX_POSITION_PERCENT=20
MAX_DAILY_LOSS_PERCENT=2
MAX_PORTFOLIO_EXPOSURE_PERCENT=80
MAX_TRADES_PER_DAY=10
MAX_SINGLE_TRADE_RISK_PERCENT=1
MAX_CORRELATED_EXPOSURE_PERCENT=35
CONSECUTIVE_LOSS_COOLDOWN_MINUTES=120

# Quotes older than this are unusable -> DO NOT TRADE.
MAX_QUOTE_STALENESS_SECONDS=120

# The composite score a signal must reach before the Risk Engine considers it.
#
# This is the bar that decides how much of the funnel ever becomes an order. If
# your run analyses events and journals decisions but never places a trade, this
# is usually why — check the dashboard funnel, which prints each refused score
# against this number.
#
# The right value is an empirical question, not a safety one: a paper run that
# never fills measures nothing, and the only way to learn where the bar belongs
# is to run it lower and let outcome tracking score the decisions. 0.30-0.35 is
# a reasonable place to start a paper run.
#
# Lowering it weakens no other limit: position caps, daily loss, exposure and
# quote staleness still apply to every order that gets through. Live mode
# refuses to boot below 0.5 — a bar lowered to see paper fills is not a bar to
# trade real money behind.
MIN_SIGNAL_SCORE=0.55

# Where `npm run study -- --out` writes what the event study measured, and where
# the agent reads it back. The book only ever blocks: a filing type measured
# drifting against a long is refused, and nothing in it can license a trade.
# No file = no opinion.
EVIDENCE_FILE=data/evidence.json

# Correlation groups, written by `npm run correlations -- --out`. These labels
# are what makes MAX_CORRELATED_EXPOSURE_PERCENT apply at all: the Risk Engine
# skips the check for an order carrying no group. No file = fall back to the
# curated sector map, which covers a dozen companies.
CORRELATION_FILE=data/correlation-groups.json

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# INGESTION
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
WATCHLIST=AAPL,MSFT,NVDA
INGEST_INTERVAL_SECONDS=60

# Feed ids from src/ingestion/feeds.ts.
#
#   (empty)  official sources only — central banks, SEC press, statistics
#            offices. These publish MACRO: rate decisions, CPI, minutes. They
#            produce market-wide events, never a company catalyst, so an agent
#            running on these alone will mostly produce WATCH and place no
#            orders. That is the pipeline working, not failing.
#   all      every feed, official and company news
#   a,b,c    exactly these ids; one that matches no feed is logged as NOT
#            running rather than silently dropped
#
# e.g. ENABLED_SOURCES=all
ENABLED_SOURCES=

# Sources to watch without trading on. An event whose EVERY source is listed
# here is ingested, detected, analysed and journalled as normal, then stopped
# before the Risk Engine — until `npm run study` has measured the category it
# falls in. One source outside the list corroborating the event lets it through.
#
# The analysis is still paid for on purpose: the journal fills with the
# decisions the source would have taken, and outcome tracking scores them. That
# buys a measured answer about a new source with LLM calls instead of capital.
#
# Promotion is automatic — no edit here once the study measures it.
# e.g. OBSERVATION_ONLY_SOURCES=news_rss,x:@someone
OBSERVATION_ONLY_SOURCES=

# May a signal be traded on the asset the MODEL named, when the event itself
# carried no ticker?
#
# Detection extracts tickers from the text. A macro, policy, sanctions or
# thematic story usually names no company at all, so the event carries no ticker
# and the analysis — however good, and already paid for — can never become an
# order: there is no symbol to price or trade.
#
# With this on, the model is shown WATCHLIST + ALLOWED_ASSETS and its chosen
# asset becomes the symbol, but ONLY if that asset is in that list. The model
# selects from your universe; it cannot extend it. Everything else is unchanged:
# the quote must still be fresh, the score must still clear MIN_SIGNAL_SCORE, and
# the Risk Engine still sizes the order and can still refuse it.
#
# Off by default, because it trades on an inference — this theme moves that
# proxy — rather than on a named subject. That belongs in a paper run first.
ALLOW_MODEL_CHOSEN_ASSET=false

# How many watched events may be analysed per cycle DESPITE falling under the
# analysis gate's confidence floor.
#
# This exists because the floor and observation want opposite things. The floor
# avoids paying an LLM call to interpret something we do not believe; for a
# source in observation, whether to believe it is the whole open question. A
# social-only event is capped at 0.35 confidence by the verifier and the floor
# is 0.50, so without this a watched X account is dropped before any analysis —
# never journalled, never scored, never promotable.
#
# It is a budget rather than a switch because each one is a paid LLM call on
# information nobody has yet shown to be worth anything. 0 restores the old
# behaviour exactly.
OBSERVATION_ANALYSIS_PER_CYCLE=3

# REQUIRED for any sec.gov request. The SEC rejects requests whose User-Agent
# lacks a contact address; without this the EDGAR adapter stays disabled.
CONTACT_EMAIL=
USER_AGENT_APP_NAME=ai-market-agent

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MARKET DATA PROVIDERS  (all optional — see docs/API_RESEARCH.md for limits,
# costs and Belgium availability before signing up for any of them)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Alpaca — free plan is IEX-only, ~200 req/min. Paper accounts are available
# worldwide; live-trading eligibility depends on country of tax residence.
ALPACA_API_KEY_ID=
ALPACA_API_SECRET_KEY=
ALPACA_DATA_FEED=iex

# Finnhub — free tier 60 calls/min, PERSONAL NON-COMMERCIAL USE ONLY.
# Historical candles require a paid plan.
#
# Setting this also turns on COMPANY NEWS ingestion, which is the only source
# here that produces company-specific events rather than macro. Every RSS feed
# in the default set publishes rate decisions and statistics; those cannot
# carry a company catalyst, so an agent without this mostly emits WATCH and
# places no orders.
#
# News reads share the 60/min budget with quotes, so the watchlist is polled a
# slice at a time — 8 symbols per cycle, wrapping around.
FINNHUB_API_KEY=

# Alpha Vantage — free tier 25 requests/DAY, 5/min. Historical fallback only.
ALPHA_VANTAGE_API_KEY=

# FRED (St. Louis Fed) — free key, 120 req/min, worldwide.
FRED_API_KEY=

# ECB Data Portal needs no key and is always enabled.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SOCIAL / X  — off by default, and billed per post read
#
# X removed its free API tier for new developers in February 2026. Every read
# costs money. Only explicitly listed accounts are polled, and no post can ever
# trigger an order on its own — posts require corroboration from an official
# source before they can influence a signal.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
ENABLE_X_INGESTION=false
X_BEARER_TOKEN=
X_MAX_POSTS_READ_PER_DAY=0
X_WATCHED_ACCOUNTS=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LLM
#
# Without a provider the system still ingests, detects and verifies events —
# it simply produces no signals. Analysis is billed per call, so this is an
# explicit opt-in.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
LLM_PROVIDER=none
LLM_MODEL=claude-opus-5
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DASHBOARD
#
# The dashboard is read-only — no endpoint can place or cancel an order — but it
# shows a live portfolio, its open positions and every signal.
#
# Loopback by default. Reaching it from another machine is a deliberate choice:
#   - for now:       keep 127.0.0.1 and forward the port
#                    ssh -N -L 3000:127.0.0.1:3000 you@your-server
#   - for a bookmark: keep 127.0.0.1 and put a tunnel in front
#                    sudo tailscale funnel --bg 3000
#   - or:            DASHBOARD_HOST=0.0.0.0 *and* a password below
#
# Startup REFUSES a non-loopback host without a password, or one under 12
# characters. A tunnel leaves the bind on loopback, so that check cannot see
# it — instead the server answers 403 to any request that arrives with a
# forwarding header or a foreign Host while no password is set. Set one before
# you tunnel. See docs/DEPLOY.md.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
DASHBOARD_PORT=3000
DASHBOARD_HOST=127.0.0.1
DASHBOARD_USER=admin
DASHBOARD_PASSWORD=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DISCORD
#
# Notifications: paste a channel webhook URL. It carries its own token — treat
# it like any other credential. Leave empty to disable.
#
# Approval: REQUIRE_APPROVAL=true asks on Discord before every order and
# REFUSES if nobody reacts within the timeout. Off by default, and not only for
# convenience — hand-approving trades during a paper run means the decision
# journal measures you rather than the strategy. Its real use is as a gate in
# front of real money.
#
# Needs a bot with Send Messages + Read Message History + Add Reactions.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL=
DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=
DISCORD_CHANNEL_ID=
REQUIRE_APPROVAL=false
APPROVAL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=300

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# INFRASTRUCTURE  (used from Phase 2 onward; docker-compose provides both)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://agent:agent@localhost:5432/market_agent
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379

HTTP_TIMEOUT_MS=10000
HTTP_MAX_RETRIES=3
